      "id": "seq-scans",
      "title": "1. Seq scans",
      "blurb": "A small shop on Postgres: logins and order history get slower as the tables grow. EXPLAIN a query to see its plan, add the indexes that help, and keep reads under 20 ms without making writes or storage pay for indexes nobody uses.",
      "hints": [
        "Look at the query cards: EXPLAIN ANALYZE shows how each one is run.",
        "A Seq Scan on a big table means no index fits the WHERE column, and every index you add costs writes and storage.",
        "Index users(email) as unique and orders(user_id), and leave the nightly report alone: it runs once."
      ],
